# The rule of this file: only SOURCE enters the repository. Nothing that can be
# generated or downloaded, nothing machine-specific and nothing secret goes in.
# The question to ask when adding a line is not "is this file a nuisance" but
# "if I deleted this from the repository, could it be produced again" and "does
# this information mean anything on somebody else's machine".

# --- build outputs: all of them are produced again by `make build` ---
/bin/
/dist/
/gobit
/server
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# --- test, coverage and profile outputs ---
#
# coverage.out can exceed 100 MB in this repository (-coverpkg=./... counts the
# whole tree); once committed, it cannot be taken out of the history.
coverage.out
coverage-integration.out
coverage.html
*.cover
*.test
*.prof
*.pprof
cpu.out
mem.out
trace.out
# A property that fails writes its draws under testdata/rapid/ (ADR 0249).
# They are printed with the failure; the file only replays them locally.
**/testdata/rapid/

# --- environment and secrets ---
#
# .env.example IS TRACKED and must stay that way: it is the only written record
# of which settings exist, and it holds no values. Every other .env is specific
# to one machine.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc

# Keys and certificates: once one goes in, it cannot be deleted from the history
# and has to be rotated. The repository needs none today; the rule is here to
# keep that absence.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*

# --- local file store (the FILE_ROOT default) ---
#
# Uploaded files do NOT enter the repository: they are user content, they do not
# belong in version control, and even a single image bloats the repository for
# good.
/data/

# --- database dumps and backups ---
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# --- editor and operating system ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- toolchain ---
#
# go.work is ONE DEVELOPER'S local multi-module setup; if it enters the
# repository, it points at paths that do not exist on somebody else's machine.
go.work
go.work.sum
node_modules/

# --- openapi client generation ---
openapi.json
clients/

# --- working notes: ON DISK, NOT IN THE REPOSITORY ---
#
# These files are a design notebook: one is the implementation plan that walks
# through the phases, the other is hand-kept architecture notes. Neither is the
# SOURCE of a decision — decisions are in docs/adr/, measurements in
# docs/gaps.md, the architecture narrative in docs/mimari.md, and all three are
# in the repository. Keeping a notebook in the repository leads everyone who
# reads it to mistake it for binding, and when it contradicts those records,
# which one wins has to be settled by a rule of its own.
#
# The third is of the same class: a feature comparison and work list. It is the
# WORKING record of what a round measured, not the decision itself — the
# decision is in the ADR, its evidence in the measurement. It came in here on
# 2026-09-13, and its reason is not only the same as the other two: as long as
# it sat untracked in the repository it also broke the language lane, because
# `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` counts it as a file of the
# repository and its content is Turkish (ADR 0012). Nor could the ledger silence
# it — that list can only SHRINK.
#
# They are NOT DELETED from disk; they only stay out of version control.
/go-commerce-framework-plan.md
/go-ecommerce-mimari.md
/gobit-ozellik-listesi.md

# The agent tooling keeps git WORKTREES here — full copies of this repository.
# They belong to no commit and must not be added to one.
.claude/worktrees/
